---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// Copy is from github.com/The-Forest-Network/the-forest-network-web/issues/6
// (comment 5650893669, compiled by wandatree from the original trial-village
// invite + subsequent discussion), with the closing note and email line updated
// in comment 6487463560. Do not edit the wording here without updating that
// issue.
---

<SiteLayout title="Join the Village">
  <article class="site-panel prose">

  <section id="poem">
    <div>
      <p class="poem">
        we need but a place<br />
        to come back to<br />
        every so often;<br />
        a small home for us<br />
        to come together;<br />
        the relief of breathing<br />
        as one, for a while,<br />
        holding and being held;<br />
        humming, too, as one<br />
        until we remember<br />
        who we are, or could be.<br />
        so that we can fly off<br />
        again, out into the world<br />
        where things are now<br />
        so achingly, unnervingly,<br />
        coming apart.
      </p>
      <p class="attribution">Moon Song, &ldquo;the starling box&rdquo;</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="calling">
    <div>
      <p>
        The Earth has been calling her
        human children to remember how
        to be in relation
        to all things;
        to be in deep relation to
        ourselves and other human beings
        and the more-than-human beings
        we share this corner of the
        galaxy with.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Forest Network is a place
        where you can connect across
        the galaxies.
        It is a place in
        which you can seek solace;
        a
        place where you can deepen into
        the Mystery&hellip; with others.
        Where you can dream and explore
        all that is and all that can be.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Village will be
        unintentional, it will be
        uncertain, allowing new forms
        of being to arise; it is a place
        where villagers are open to
        the eddies of mystery;
        where we
        can allow the Village itself to
        be a participating being
        in the
        creation of the village tapestry
        within the global tapestry.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="invitation">
    <div>
      <p>
        If this invitation calls to your heart, please share with us what&rsquo;s drawing you
        through the fungal hyphae and into The Forest Network, and a little about yourself and
        your journey to date so that we can get to know you better. Here&rsquo;s a few ideas:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Poetry that expresses something deep inside</li>
        <li>Experiences you&rsquo;ve had in nature</li>
        <li>Dreams</li>
        <li>Art</li>
        <li>Imagery</li>
        <li>Recorded video/audio</li>
        <li>Collages</li>
        <li>Photographs</li>
        <li>Your deepest desires and fears</li>
        <li>Work you&rsquo;ve done in nature (rituals, remembrances, awakenings, healing, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Also include a paragraph expressing what you hope to find in the clearing created by
        The Forest Network Village.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please be concise, you are making your first introduction to the Village. We suggest
        what fits into 5 minutes of reading/listening/looking &mdash; eg 2 pages of written
        text, 5 minutes of audio, 2 images&hellip; Once you are part of the Village you will
        have ample opportunity to share as much as you wish.
      </p>
      <p>All submissions will be held close to our hearts and in strict confidence!</p>
      <p>
        <b><i>Note: This step is needed to come into the Village, even if you've downloaded the mobile apps already.
        We have erected this village gate to protect the intentions, purpose, and solidarity of our
        villagers.</i></b>
      </p>
      <p>If you have any questions, please don&rsquo;t hesitate to write to <a class="write-link"
        href="mailto:trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth?subject=Join%20the%20Village"
        >trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .prose section + section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(212, 232, 172, 0.2);
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .poem {
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem);
  }

  .attribution {
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #d4e8ac;
  }

  .write-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
</style>
